                <text type="synoptic_situation">A cold front clears to the east Wednesday evening. Weak troughs clip the southeast in a broad westerly flow on Thursday and Friday, as a ridge of high pressure is expected to approach South Australia from the west. The high centre is expected to linger over the state on the weekend.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
